course: dictionary
lesson: 8306
title: Roadhog and road manners
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A roadhog is a noun for a selfish, dangerous road user. It is someone who drives too fast or takes up so much of the road that other people cannot pass. The word is built from road and hog. A hog is a pig, so the word calls the driver greedy, like a pig that will not share.
explain: Context gives clues. In a story, the Rat shakes his fists at a car that has gone and shouts, «You villains! ... you roadhogs!» Villains are bad people, so the Rat is angry at bad drivers. A roadhog is a driver who does not care about anyone else on the road.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad falls in love with motor cars, drives wildly, crashes, and is called a «road-hog» and worse at his trial. Good drivers share the road. A roadhog ignores other road users, and that is why the word is an insult.
fact: A roadhog is a selfish, dangerous driver who takes up too much of the road.
fact: The word can also describe anyone, such as a cyclist, who acts as if the road belongs only to them.
fact: A hog is a pig, so the word suggests the driver is greedy.
fact: «You roadhogs!» is a shout of anger in The Wind in the Willows.
fact: Early motorists in the 1900s were often blamed for frightening horses and people.
exercise: The Rat shouts, «You villains! ... you roadhogs!» What is a roadhog? | A kind driver who stops to help | A pig that lives on a farm | A bus with a loud horn | *A selfish, dangerous driver who takes too much of the road
exercise: Why does the word hog suit a roadhog? | Because hogs always wear helmets | *Because a hog is a pig, so it calls the driver greedy | Because hogs are very fast runners | Because hogs have long horns
exercise: Good drivers share the road. What does a roadhog do instead? | Stops to help the horses | Waves the cyclists on | *Ignores other road users | Lets others pass safely
test: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad becomes a roadhog after he falls in love with what? | *Motor cars | Boats | Horses | Trains
test: Which is the best description of a roadhog? | *A driver who ignores other road users | A farmer who walks his pigs | A driver who waves others past | A cyclist who signals every turn
exam: Which word means a selfish, dangerous road user who ignores others? | glum | barely | *roadhog | ancient
